      source: "Line engraving of Evangelista Torricelli in an oval frame with the legend 'En virescit Galilaeus alter. Anagr. Evangelista Torricellius Serenissimi M. Ducis Herruriae Mathem.cus & Philos.us Obijt Anno Dom. MDCXLVII Aet. XL' and a signature ending 'Anichinius f.'; Wellcome Collection, work fgrk8gye (reference 9219i, image V0005861), catalogued 'Evangelista Torricelli. Line engraving by P. Anichini', dated 1640-1649, contributor 'Anichini, Pietro, 1610-1645'. The file is a crop of the oval portrait from the holder's 2439 x 3264 pixel IIIF image, downscaled from 1780 x 2089 to 852 x 1000 with no upscaling. The legend records his death in 1647, so the plate was cut after October 1647 (or the legend added to an earlier plate), which sits uneasily with the catalogued engraver dates; the same engraved portrait is described in the DSB as reproduced on the frontispiece of the 1715 Lezioni accademiche.",
