      source: "Detail of Jacques-Louis David, 'Antoine Laurent Lavoisier (1743-1794) and Marie Anne Lavoisier (Marie Anne Pierrette Paulze, 1758-1836)', 1788, oil on canvas, 259.7 x 194.6 cm, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, accession 1977.10 (Purchase, Mr. and Mrs. Charles Wrightsman Gift, in honor of Everett Fahy, 1977), Open Access image DP-19709-001 (3038 x 4000). The file is a 740 x 850 pixel crop of the female sitter's head and shoulders cut from the Met's original image at full resolution: cropped only, not resized, not upscaled.",
