      // [src_ricci_ncatholic, src_ricci_wang | 1589-1614 | reference biography, journal article] The Jesuit strategy of winning the learned first and moving north from the provinces to Nanjing and Beijing was set by the Jesuit visitor Valignano and carried out by Ricci (New Catholic Encyclopedia); Wang shows a sequenced programme in which mathematics, then Euclid, then further mathematical books prepared the ground for religious teaching, drawing on his own stated reasoning. The plan was shared and his reasoning is largely his own testimony. CONCENTRATION (agent): lowered from 70 / 0.56 for shared credit and reliance on his own statements.
